arsing: Who Did What to Whom","stamp":"DEPENDENCY PARSING: WHO DID WHAT TO WHOM","topic":""},{"id":"u3-03","number":13,"name":"Transition-Based Parsing: Building Trees Step by Step","stamp":"TRANSITION-BASED PARSING: BUILDING TREES STEP BY STEP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-01","number":14,"name":"Word Vectors: Giving Words a Place on a Map","stamp":"WORD VECTORS: GIVING WORDS A PLACE ON A MAP","topic":""},{"id":"u4-02","number":15,"name":"Word2Vec: Learning Word Vectors from Context","stamp":"WORD2VEC: LEARNING WORD VECTORS FROM CONTEXT","topic":""},{"id":"u4-03","number":16,"name":"Recurrent Neural Networks: Reading with Memory","stamp":"RECURRENT NEURAL NETWORKS: READING WITH MEMORY","topic":""},{"id":"u4-04","number":17,"name":"LSTMs: Remembering What Matters","stamp":"LSTMS: REMEMBERING WHAT MATTERS","topic":""},{"id":"u5-01","number":18,"name":"Contextual Embeddings and ELMo","stamp":"CONTEXTUAL EMBEDDINGS AND ELMO","topic":""},{"id":"u5-02","number":19,"name":"BERT: Reading in Both Directions","stamp":"BERT: READING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS","topic":""}]},"stop":{"number":16,"name":"Recurrent Neural Networks: Reading with Memory","stamp":"RECURRENT NEURAL NETWORKS: READING WITH MEMORY"},"shorts":{"width":1080,"height":1920,"maxSeconds":60,"cta":"Full lesson: NLP, Simply Explained · Unit 4"},"thumbnail":{"headline":"How AI reads with memory","big":"the → cat → sat"},"segments":[{"id":"intro","kind":"intro","component":"TitleCard","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c01","start":0.6,"end":8.241,"marks":{},"text":"Welcome back to NLP, Simply Explained. This is unit 4, lesson 3: recurrent neural networks, or RNNs.","words":[{"w":"Welcome","start":0.6},{"w":"back","start":1.08},{"w":"to","start":1.427},{"w":"NLP,","start":1.773},{"w":"Simply","start":2.12},{"w":"Explained.","start":2.72},{"w":"This","start":3.56},{"w":"is","start":3.84},{"w":"unit","start":4.04},{"w":"4,","start":4.44},{"w":"lesson","start":4.84},{"w":"3:","start":5.24},{"w":"recurrent","start":5.64},{"w":"neural","start":6.2},{"w":"networks,","start":6.71},{"w":"or","start":7.22},{"w":"RNNs.","start":7.731}]},{"id":"c02","start":8.641,"end":17.016,"marks":{},"text":"Word vectors give each word a meaning. But a sentence is more than a bag of words: order matters. Today we meet a network that reads in order.","words":[{"w":"Word","start":8.921},{"w":"vectors","start":9.201},{"w":"give","start":9.481},{"w":"each","start":9.681},{"w":"word","start":9.921},{"w":"a","start":10.161},{"w":"meaning.","start":10.321},{"w":"But","start":10.841},{"w":"a","start":11.041},{"w":"sentence","start":11.241},{"w":"is","start":11.801},{"w":"more","start":12.041},{"w":"than","start":12.241},{"w":"a","start":12.401},{"w":"bag","start":12.561},{"w":"of","start":12.801},{"w":"words:","start":12.961},{"w":"order","start":13.481},{"w":"matters.","start":13.921},{"w":"Today","start":14.461},{"w":"we","start":15.001},{"w":"meet","start":15.201},{"w":"a","start":15.401},{"w":"network","start":15.481},{"w":"that","start":15.921},{"w":"reads","start":16.081},{"w":"in","start":16.441},{"w":"order.","start":16.641}]}],"title":"Welcome","shortTitle":"Welcome","props":{"kicker":"Unit 4 · Lesson 3","title":"Recurrent Neural Networks","subtitle":"Reading with memory"},"start":0.6,"end":17.016,"startFrame":0,"durationInFrames":538},{"id":"idea","kind":"core","component":"BigIdea","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c03","start":17.933,"end":25.498,"marks":{},"text":"Here's the idea. A recurrent neural network reads one word at a time, and carries a memory forward from each word to the next.","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":17.933},{"w":"the","start":18.333},{"w":"idea.","start":18.493},{"w":"A","start":19.213},{"w":"recurrent","start":19.413},{"w":"neural","start":19.873},{"w":"network","start":20.333},{"w":"reads","start":20.813},{"w":"one","start":21.213},{"w":"word","start":21.453},{"w":"at","start":21.693},{"w":"a","start":21.853},{"w":"time,","start":22.013},{"w":"and","start":22.373},{"w":"carries","start":22.573},{"w":"a","start":23.053},{"w":"memory","start":23.173},{"w":"forward","start":23.653},{"w":"from","start":24.053},{"w":"each","start":24.253},{"w":"word","start":24.573},{"w":"to","start":24.773},{"w":"the","start":24.933},{"w":"next.","start":25.053}]}],"title":"The big idea","shortTitle":"The big idea","props":{"kicker":"Key idea","text":"An RNN reads one word at a time, and carries a memory forward.","highlight":["memory"]},"start":17.933,"end":25.498,"startFrame":538,"durationInFrames":254},{"id":"rnn","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c04","start":26.4,"end":35.885,"marks":{},"text":"RNN stands for recurrent neural network. It reads a sequence step by step, and passes a hidden state, a kind of memory, from each step to the next.","words":[{"w":"RNN","start":26.76},{"w":"stands","start":27.12},{"w":"for","start":27.48},{"w":"recurrent","start":27.68},{"w":"neural","start":28.16},{"w":"network.","start":28.52},{"w":"It","start":29.24},{"w":"reads","start":29.44},{"w":"a","start":29.84},{"w":"sequence","start":30},{"w":"step","start":30.48},{"w":"by","start":30.84},{"w":"step,","start":31.04},{"w":"and","start":31.44},{"w":"passes","start":31.68},{"w":"a","start":32.16},{"w":"hidden","start":32.32},{"w":"state,","start":32.72},{"w":"a","start":33.12},{"w":"kind","start":33.36},{"w":"of","start":33.56},{"w":"memory,","start":33.72},{"w":"from","start":34.28},{"w":"each","start":34.48},{"w":"step","start":34.84},{"w":"to","start":35.16},{"w":"the","start":35.32},{"w":"next.","start":35.44}]},{"id":"c05","start":36.285,"end":41.861,"marks":{},"text":"Reading \"the cat sat\", it updates its memory after the, again after cat, and again after sat.","words":[{"w":"Reading","start":36.285},{"w":"\"the","start":36.685},{"w":"cat","start":36.845},{"w":"sat\",","start":37.125},{"w":"it","start":37.525},{"w":"updates","start":37.725},{"w":"its","start":38.245},{"w":"memory","start":38.485},{"w":"after","start":38.925},{"w":"the,","start":39.245},{"w":"again","start":39.565},{"w":"after","start":39.925},{"w":"cat,","start":40.245},{"w":"and","start":40.565},{"w":"again","start":40.765},{"w":"after","start":41.125},{"w":"sat.","start":41.445}]},{"id":"c06","start":42.261,"end":48.006,"marks":{},"text":"Think of reading a book while keeping a running summary in your head. Each new sentence updates the summary.","words":[{"w":"Think","start":42.261},{"w":"of","start":42.421},{"w":"reading","start":42.581},{"w":"a","start":42.901},{"w":"book","start":43.061},{"w":"while","start":43.341},{"w":"keeping","start":43.541},{"w":"a","start":43.861},{"w":"running","start":44.021},{"w":"summary","start":44.421},{"w":"in","start":44.861},{"w":"your","start":45.021},{"w":"head.","start":45.261},{"w":"Each","start":45.701},{"w":"new","start":46.061},{"w":"sentence","start":46.301},{"w":"updates","start":46.821},{"w":"the","start":47.381},{"w":"summary.","start":47.501}]}],"title":"What is an RNN?","shortTitle":"What is an RNN?","props":{"kicker":"Definition","term":"RNN","definition":"Recurrent neural network: reads a sequence step by step, passing a hidden state, its memory, from each step to the next.","example":"the → cat → sat: memory updated at every word","analogy":"Reading a book while keeping a running summary in your head."},"start":26.4,"end":48.006,"startFrame":792,"durationInFrames":676},{"id":"step","kind":"core","component":"Steps","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c07","start":48.933,"end":51.135,"marks":{},"text":"Here's what happens at every single word.","words":[{"w":"Here's","start":49.093},{"w":"what","start":49.253},{"w":"happens","start":49.453},{"w":"at","start":49.893},{"w":"every","start":50.053},{"w":"single","start":50.293},{"w":"word.","start":50.813}]},{"id":"c08","start":51.535,"end":53.803,"marks":{},"text":"Read: take the vector for the next word.","words":[{"w":"Read:","start":51.535},{"w":"take","start":52.015},{"w":"the","start":52.295},{"w":"vector","start":52.575},{"w":"for","start":52.855},{"w":"the","start":52.975},{"w":"next","start":53.135},{"w":"word.","start":53.495}]},{"id":"c09","start":54.203,"end":57.921,"marks":{},"text":"Combine: mix it with the memory carried over from the previous step.","words":[{"w":"Combine:","start":54.203},{"w":"mix","start":54.923},{"w":"it","start":55.283},{"w":"with","start":55.443},{"w":"the","start":55.603},{"w":"memory","start":55.723},{"w":"carried","start":56.203},{"w":"over","start":56.563},{"w":"from","start":56.763},{"w":"the","start":56.923},{"w":"previous","start":57.043},{"w":"step.","start":57.563}]},{"id":"c10","start":58.321,"end":60.639,"marks":{},"text":"Update: that mix becomes the new memory.","words":[{"w":"Update:","start":58.621},{"w":"that","start":58.921},{"w":"mix","start":59.161},{"w":"becomes","start":59.441},{"w":"the","start":59.881},{"w":"new","start":60.001},{"w":"memory.","start":60.161}]},{"id":"c11","start":61.039,"end":68.417,"marks":{},"text":"Output: if needed, use the memory to produce something, like a guess for the next word. Then move on, and do it all again.","words":[{"w":"Output:","start":61.039},{"w":"if","start":61.599},{"w":"needed,","start":61.839},{"w":"use","start":62.359},{"w":"the","start":62.639},{"w":"memory","start":62.799},{"w":"to","start":63.199},{"w":"produce","start":63.319},{"w":"something,","start":63.799},{"w":"like","start":64.159},{"w":"a","start":64.399},{"w":"guess","start":64.519},{"w":"for","start":64.879},{"w":"the","start":64.999},{"w":"next","start":65.159},{"w":"word.","start":65.559},{"w":"Then","start":66.039},{"w":"move","start":66.399},{"w":"on,","start":66.799},{"w":"and","start":67.039},{"w":"do","start":67.279},{"w":"it","start":67.519},{"w":"all","start":67.759},{"w":"again.","start":67.999}]}],"title":"One step of an RNN","shortTitle":"One step of an RNN","props":{"kicker":"Inside one step","title":"What happens at every word","steps":[{"label":"Read","detail":"the next word's vector"},{"label":"Combine","detail":"it with the memory so far"},{"label":"Update","detail":"write the new memory"},{"label":"Output","detail":"e.g. a guess for the next word"}]},"start":48.933,"end":68.417,"startFrame":1468,"durationInFrames":612},{"id":"vs","kind":"core","component":"Compare","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c12","start":69.333,"end":72.951,"marks":{},"text":"Why is this better than the n-gram language models from unit one?","words":[{"w":"Why","start":69.333},{"w":"is","start":69.573},{"w":"this","start":69.813},{"w":"better","start":70.093},{"w":"than","start":70.413},{"w":"the","start":70.613},{"w":"n-gram","start":70.773},{"w":"language","start":71.293},{"w":"models","start":71.733},{"w":"from","start":72.133},{"w":"unit","start":72.293},{"w":"one?","start":72.653}]},{"id":"c13","start":73.351,"end":81.282,"marks":{},"text":"An n-gram model only looks back a fixed few words, and counts exact sequences, so it knows nothing about phrases it never saw.","words":[{"w":"An","start":73.351},{"w":"n-gram","start":73.511},{"w":"model","start":74.071},{"w":"only","start":74.551},{"w":"looks","start":74.831},{"w":"back","start":75.111},{"w":"a","start":75.351},{"w":"fixed","start":75.511},{"w":"few","start":75.871},{"w":"words,","start":76.191},{"w":"and","start":76.631},{"w":"counts","start":76.911},{"w":"exact","start":77.351},{"w":"sequences,","start":77.831},{"w":"so","start":78.591},{"w":"it","start":78.791},{"w":"knows","start":79.031},{"w":"nothing","start":79.351},{"w":"about","start":79.671},{"w":"phrases","start":79.911},{"w":"it","start":80.471},{"w":"never","start":80.671},{"w":"saw.","start":80.951}]},{"id":"c14","start":81.682,"end":91.276,"marks":{},"text":"An RNN's memory can, in principle, hold the whole sentence so far. And because it works with word vectors, what it learns about rain also helps with storm.","words":[{"w":"An","start":81.989},{"w":"RNN's","start":82.295},{"w":"memory","start":82.602},{"w":"can,","start":83.082},{"w":"in","start":83.362},{"w":"principle,","start":83.522},{"w":"hold","start":84.242},{"w":"the","start":84.562},{"w":"whole","start":84.722},{"w":"sentence","start":84.962},{"w":"so","start":85.522},{"w":"far.","start":85.762},{"w":"And","start":86.162},{"w":"because","start":86.482},{"w":"it","start":86.802},{"w":"works","start":86.962},{"w":"with","start":87.322},{"w":"word","start":87.695},{"w":"vectors,","start":88.069},{"w":"what","start":88.442},{"w":"it","start":88.642},{"w":"learns","start":88.802},{"w":"about","start":89.162},{"w":"rain","start":89.402},{"w":"also","start":89.842},{"w":"helps","start":90.162},{"w":"with","start":90.602},{"w":"storm.","start":90.762}]}],"title":"Why not n-grams?","shortTitle":"Why not n-grams?","props":{"kicker":"A step up","title":"N-gram model versus RNN","columns":[{"title":"N-gram model","items":["looks back a fixed few words","counts exact word sequences"],"tone":"neutral"},{"title":"RNN","items":["memory can hold the whole sentence so far","uses word vectors: similar words help each other"],"tone":"good"}],"verdict":{"text":"No fixed window: the memory decides"}},"start":69.333,"end":91.276,"startFrame":2080,"durationInFrames":686},{"id":"uses","kind":"core","component":"Bullets","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c15","start":92.2,"end":96.434,"marks":{},"text":"Before today's models arrived, RNNs powered much of NLP.","words":[{"w":"Before","start":92.2},{"w":"today's","start":92.56},{"w":"models","start":92.92},{"w":"arrived,","start":93.6},{"w":"RNNs","start":94.28},{"w":"powered","start":94.96},{"w":"much","start":95.36},{"w":"of","start":95.718},{"w":"NLP.","start":96.076}]},{"id":"c16","start":96.834,"end":99.064,"marks":{},"text":"Language models, guessing the next word.","words":[{"w":"Language","start":96.834},{"w":"models,","start":97.314},{"w":"guessing","start":97.834},{"w":"the","start":98.274},{"w":"next","start":98.394},{"w":"word.","start":98.754}]},{"id":"c17","start":99.464,"end":102.809,"marks":{},"text":"Tagging, giving every word a label, like a part of speech.","words":[{"w":"Tagging,","start":99.464},{"w":"giving","start":100.024},{"w":"every","start":100.424},{"w":"word","start":100.664},{"w":"a","start":100.944},{"w":"label,","start":101.104},{"w":"like","start":101.584},{"w":"a","start":101.784},{"w":"part","start":101.944},{"w":"of","start":102.144},{"w":"speech.","start":102.264}]},{"id":"c18","start":103.209,"end":110.057,"marks":{},"text":"And translation: one RNN reads a sentence in one language, and another writes it out in a different language.","words":[{"w":"And","start":103.209},{"w":"translation:","start":103.409},{"w":"one","start":104.156},{"w":"RNN","start":104.902},{"w":"reads","start":105.649},{"w":"a","start":105.969},{"w":"sentence","start":106.089},{"w":"in","start":106.569},{"w":"one","start":106.769},{"w":"language,","start":106.969},{"w":"and","start":107.529},{"w":"another","start":107.769},{"w":"writes","start":108.169},{"w":"it","start":108.609},{"w":"out","start":108.769},{"w":"in","start":108.929},{"w":"a","start":109.049},{"w":"different","start":109.129},{"w":"language.","start":109.529}]}],"title":"What RNNs are used for","shortTitle":"What RNNs are used for","props":{"kicker":"Uses","title":"What RNNs were used for","items":[{"text":"Language models: guess the next word"},{"text":"Tagging: a label for every word"},{"text":"Translation: read one language, write another"}],"numbered":false},"start":92.2,"end":110.057,"startFrame":2766,"durationInFrames":563},{"id":"train","kind":"core","component":"Definition","short":false,"cues":[{"id":"c19","start":110.967,"end":124.28,"marks":{},"text":"How does an RNN learn? With a method called backpropagation through time. Picture the network unrolled across all the words. We measure its error, then send that error backwards through every step, adjusting the weights a little.","words":[{"w":"How","start":110.967},{"w":"does","start":111.127},{"w":"an","start":111.327},{"w":"RNN","start":111.727},{"w":"learn?","start":112.127},{"w":"With","start":112.487},{"w":"a","start":112.727},{"w":"method","start":112.847},{"w":"called","start":113.247},{"w":"backpropagation","start":113.947},{"w":"through","start":114.647},{"w":"time.","start":114.967},{"w":"Picture","start":115.567},{"w":"the","start":116.127},{"w":"network","start":116.327},{"w":"unrolled","start":116.847},{"w":"across","start":117.407},{"w":"all","start":117.847},{"w":"the","start":118.047},{"w":"words.","start":118.207},{"w":"We","start":118.727},{"w":"measure","start":118.967},{"w":"its","start":119.314},{"w":"error,","start":119.66},{"w":"then","start":120.007},{"w":"send","start":120.247},{"w":"that","start":120.567},{"w":"error","start":120.887},{"w":"backwards","start":121.207},{"w":"through","start":121.767},{"w":"every","start":122.007},{"w":"step,","start":122.327},{"w":"adjusting","start":122.767},{"w":"the","start":123.367},{"w":"weights","start":123.527},{"w":"a","start":123.887},{"w":"little.","start":124.047}]},{"id":"c20","start":124.68,"end":128.874,"marks":{},"text":"So a mistake at word ten can send blame all the way back to word one.","words":[{"w":"So","start":124.68},{"w":"a","start":124.8},{"w":"mistake","start":124.92},{"w":"at","start":125.36},{"w":"word","start":125.52},{"w":"ten","start":125.8},{"w":"can","start":126.28},{"w":"send","start":126.52},{"w":"blame","start":126.84},{"w":"all","start":127.28},{"w":"the","start":127.44},{"w":"way","start":127.56},{"w":"back","start":127.8},{"w":"to","start":128.08},{"w":"word","start":128.28},{"w":"one.","start":128.56}]},{"id":"c21","start":129.274,"end":134.761,"marks":{},"text":"It's like replaying a chess game move by move, to find which early move really cost you the game.","words":[{"w":"It's","start":129.274},{"w":"like","start":129.474},{"w":"replaying","start":129.634},{"w":"a","start":130.194},{"w":"chess","start":130.314},{"w":"game","start":130.674},{"w":"move","start":130.994},{"w":"by","start":131.314},{"w":"move,","start":131.514},{"w":"to","start":131.914},{"w":"find","start":132.154},{"w":"which","start":132.474},{"w":"early","start":132.714},{"w":"move","start":133.114},{"w":"really","start":133.434},{"w":"cost","start":133.794},{"w":"you","start":134.154},{"w":"the","start":134.274},{"w":"game.","start":134.434}]}],"title":"How an RNN learns","shortTitle":"How an RNN learns","props":{"kicker":"Training","term":"Backpropagation through time","definition":"Unroll the network across the words, measure the error, then send it backwards through every step to adjust the weights.","example":"a mistake at word 10 → blame flows back to word 1","analogy":"Replaying a game move by move, to find which early move cost you."},"start":110.967,"end":134.761,"startFrame":3329,"durationInFrames":741},{"id":"forget","kind":"core","component":"Bullets","short":true,"cues":[{"id":"c22","start":135.667,"end":148.892,"marks":{},"text":"But there's a catch, known as the vanishing gradient problem. Take: \"The keys that I left on the kitchen table yesterday are missing.\" To choose \"are\" rather than \"is\", the network must remember \"keys\" from far back.","words":[{"w":"But","start":135.667},{"w":"there's","start":135.787},{"w":"a","start":136.067},{"w":"catch,","start":136.227},{"w":"known","start":136.627},{"w":"as","start":137.027},{"w":"the","start":137.227},{"w":"vanishing","start":137.347},{"w":"gradient","start":137.987},{"w":"problem.","start":138.547},{"w":"Take:","start":139.347},{"w":"\"The","start":139.787},{"w":"keys","start":140.147},{"w":"that","start":140.587},{"w":"I","start":140.747},{"w":"left","start":140.947},{"w":"on","start":141.147},{"w":"the","start":141.267},{"w":"kitchen","start":141.387},{"w":"table","start":141.787},{"w":"yesterday","start":142.147},{"w":"are","start":142.747},{"w":"missing.\"","start":142.907},{"w":"To","start":143.627},{"w":"choose","start":143.947},{"w":"\"are\"","start":144.507},{"w":"rather","start":144.787},{"w":"than","start":145.147},{"w":"\"is\",","start":145.387},{"w":"the","start":145.747},{"w":"network","start":145.947},{"w":"must","start":146.547},{"w":"remember","start":146.747},{"w":"\"keys\"","start":147.347},{"w":"from","start":147.867},{"w":"far","start":148.107},{"w":"back.","start":148.467}]},{"id":"c23","start":149.292,"end":153.684,"marks":{},"text":"The trouble is that the learning signal fades a little at every step it travels back.","words":[{"w":"The","start":149.292},{"w":"trouble","start":149.412},{"w":"is","start":149.772},{"w":"that","start":149.972},{"w":"the","start":150.092},{"w":"learning","start":150.252},{"w":"signal","start":150.652},{"w":"fades","start":151.132},{"w":"a","start":151.532},{"w":"little","start":151.692},{"w":"at","start":151.932},{"w":"every","start":152.092},{"w":"step","start":152.332},{"w":"it","start":152.692},{"w":"travels","start":152.852},{"w":"back.","start":153.412}]},{"id":"c24","start":154.084,"end":156.434,"marks":{},"text":"After many words, it has almost vanished.","words":[{"w":"After","start":154.084},{"w":"many","start":154.404},{"w":"words,","start":154.724},{"w":"it","start":155.124},{"w":"has","start":155.284},{"w":"almost","start":155.484},{"w":"vanished.","start":155.844}]},{"id":"c25","start":156.834,"end":162.917,"marks":{},"text":"So plain RNNs struggle to remember the start of long sentences. Next lesson fixes this.","words":[{"w":"So","start":156.834},{"w":"plain","start":157.074},{"w":"RNNs","start":157.754},{"w":"struggle","start":158.434},{"w":"to","start":158.874},{"w":"remember","start":158.994},{"w":"the","start":159.394},{"w":"start","start":159.554},{"w":"of","start":159.874},{"w":"long","start":160.034},{"w":"sentences.","start":160.314},{"w":"Next","start":160.901},{"w":"lesson","start":161.487},{"w":"fixes","start":162.074},{"w":"this.","start":162.634}]}],"title":"The forgetting problem","shortTitle":"Why early AI forgot the start of sentences","props":{"kicker":"The catch","title":"The forgetting problem","items":[{"text":"The learning signal fades at every step back"},{"t